<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rozvi Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rozvi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rozvi Empire was a state on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a> that emerged in the late seventeenth century under the Changamire dynasty, after breaking away from and overshadowing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> state. Its economy rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-based patronage, the gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> trade and tribute from a predominantly Shona-speaking population. It was weakened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> migrations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfecane">Mfecane</a> in the nineteenth century and collapsed after the death of the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changamire">Changamire</a> in about 1836.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire.jpg" alt="Rozvi Empire" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ypirétis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empire-rozvi.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 1680s and 1690s the <b>Rozvi</b> state under Changamire Dombo supplanted Mutapa authority across much of the plateau and drove the Portuguese from their inland trading posts.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 1680s Changamire Dombo, a former Mutapa herder-general, overthrew the Torwa and founded the <b>Rozvi</b> state on the same lands.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-butua">Kingdom of Butua</a></li></ul></section>
